;; What this case exercises; edit by hand.  `bb corpus-accept' leaves it alone.
(:book "A new reference grammar of modern Spanish (2019)"
 :source "Espanol/A new reference grammar of modern Spanish (2019).pdf"
 :page 64
 :exercises "Future-work 11 evidence: aligned example pairs.  Usage examples set
Spanish on the left and the English rendering on the right, two-cell
rows with source citations ((CORPES, Arg.)).  The zone repair joins
some rows with tabs where baselines align and the rest interleave -
a Spanish line, its English mate a line late.  Two-cell row
detection is the FW11 fix; this golden records the current braid
deliberately.  The dropped line is the folio-merged running head.
The budget is the pair interleaving, all nine breaks inside the
example blocks."
 :budget (:mid-sentence 9))
